+       * draws read. After a plain write lock, the draws that follow copy the
+       * vertices they read into the stream uploader at the draw. Copying
+       * every write lock's whole range at Unlock instead took a 4 MiB copy
+       * for each of Valley's whole-buffer locks, about 400 MB/s, and ran
+       * the 32-bit process out of address space (docs/f6va.md). */
+      if (sub->transfer_write && sub->transfer_plain &&
+          resource->flags.VertexBuffer &&
